-- title:
--   §3.1, p.6 — every line-search Frank-Wolfe sequence from $C_0$ alternates $x_t = C_t$, $B_t$, so $\langle x_t, e_1\rangle = (-1)^t/4$
-- statement:
--   Let $f$, $(\eta_\ell)$ be given by Theorem 3.1 for the sketches $\mathcal P_k$ of §3.1, the vertices $V_k$ ($C_k$ for even $k$, $B_k$ for odd $k$), directions $(u_k)$ chosen as on p.6, some admissible $(\delta_\ell)$, an open convex $\mathcal D$ containing the triangle $\mathcal C=\operatorname{conv}\{(-1,0),(0,1),(1,0)\}$, and $d\ge2$. Then $\operatorname{arg\,min}_{\mathcal C}f=\bigcap_k\mathcal P_k$, and every sequence generated by the Frank-Wolfe algorithm on $\mathcal C$ with the line-search strategy (iii) from $x_0=C_0$ satisfies, for all $t\in\mathbb N$,
--   $$
--   x_t=\begin{cases}C_t&\text{if $t$ is even;}\\ B_t&\text{if $t$ is odd,}\end{cases}\qquad\text{hence}\qquad \langle x_t,e_1\rangle=\frac{(-1)^t}{4},
--   $$
--
--   and therefore $(x_t)_{t\in\mathbb N}$ does not converge.
--
--   This is the trajectory that makes the iterates of Counterexample 3.5 oscillate between abscissae $1/4$ and $-1/4$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "f defined via Theorem 3.1" is `IsSketch` plus `IsInterpolant` for these data; $\mathcal P_0\subset\mathcal D$ follows from (v). Every oracle selection and every line-search minimizer is covered.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - generalization: the p.6 display (x_t = C_t or B_t and ⟨x_t, e₁⟩ = (−1)^t/4) → also the p.5 claim arg min_C f = ⋂ₖ Pₖ, under the same hypotheses; reason: an added conclusion from the same construction; dropping it gives the display
--   - encoding: "f be defined via Theorem 3.1" with the §3.1 data and (u_k) as on p.6 → hypotheses IsSketch sketchPolygon sketchVertex u δ (corrected), IsDirectionChoice u and IsInterpolant D d sketchPolygon sketchVertex u δ f η, for any δ, any open convex D ⊇ C and any d ≥ 2; reason: the data and conclusions of Theorem 3.1 for this instance
--   - encoding: "any sequence generated by Frank-Wolfe with (iii)" from x₀ = C₀ → every x with IsFWRun triangle f (lineSearch f) (sketchC 0) x; reason: Remark 2.2(i): every oracle selection and every line-search minimizer
--   - encoding: f : D → ℝ → f : ℝ² → ℝ with every property (convexity, smoothness, sublevel sets, gradient, Hessian) required on D only; reason: the values of f outside D never enter; D is open, so gradients and Hessians at points of D are the true ones
-- source:
--   Bolte, Combettes & Pauwels, The Iterates of the Frank-Wolfe Algorithm May Not Converge, arXiv:2202.08711v1, §3.1, p.6, display "Let x0 = C0. By induction and using Lemma 3.3 …"; and p.5, "The solution set is arg minC f = ⋂k∈N Pk"

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FWIterates_IsFWRun
import Definitions.Def_FWIterates_IsSketch
import Definitions.Def_FWIterates_IsInterpolant
import Definitions.Def_FWIterates_sketchPoints

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace
open Filter Topology

namespace FWIterates

/-- **The trajectory of §3.1** (arXiv:2202.08711v1, §3.1, display "Let x0 = C0. By induction",
p.6). Let `f`, `η` be produced by Theorem 3.1 for the sketches `P_k` of §3.1, the vertices
`V_k = C_k` (`k` even), `V_k = B_k` (`k` odd), directions `(u_k)` chosen as on p.6, any admissible
`(δ ℓ)`, an open convex `D` containing the triangle `C = conv{(−1, 0), (0, 1), (1, 0)}`, and
`d ≥ 2`. Then every sequence generated by the Frank-Wolfe algorithm on `C` with the line-search
rule (iii) from `x₀ = C₀` satisfies, for all `t`, `xₜ = C_t` if `t` is even and `xₜ = B_t` if `t`
is odd, and therefore `⟨xₜ, e₁⟩ = (−1)^t/4`, so `(xₜ)` does not converge. Moreover (p.5) the solution set is
`argmin_C f = ⋂ k, P_k`.

**Formalization Note** "f defined via Theorem 3.1" is `IsSketch` (the corrected hypotheses) plus
`IsInterpolant` (its conclusions) for these data. `P₀ ⊆ D`, which Theorem 3.1 needs, follows from
clause (v) of `IsInterpolant`. Every oracle selection and every line-search minimizer is covered. -/
theorem section_3_1_trajectory (u : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) (δ : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hS : IsSketch sketchPolygon sketchVertex u δ) (hu : IsDirectionChoice u)
    (D : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2))) (hD : IsOpen D) (hDc : Convex ℝ D) (hCD : triangle ⊆ D)
    (d : ℕ) (hd : 2 ≤ d) (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2) → ℝ) (η : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hI : IsInterpolant D d sketchPolygon sketchVertex u δ f η)
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) (hx : IsFWRun triangle f (lineSearch f) (sketchC 0) x) :
    {z | z ∈ triangle ∧ ∀ y ∈ triangle, f z ≤ f y} = ⋂ k, sketchPolygon k ∧
      (∀ t : ℕ, x t = sketchVertex t ∧ ⟪x t, e₁⟫ = (-1 : ℝ) ^ t / 4) ∧
      ¬ ∃ z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2), Tendsto x atTop (𝓝 z) := by sorry

end FWIterates
